  },
  data: {
    LLM: "After the deal, bidding starts with the player to dealer's left. Each player may bid once (or pass). Bids in ascending order: Question, IsIt, Kicker, Having the Ladies, Solo, IsIt Solo, 6 Trick Solo, Bronco, Bull Solo, Solo 2. Highest bidder becomes declarer; in some bids the declarer calls an ace (not in hand) and its holder is partner. Trump is determined by the bid (e.g. Solo: declarer chooses; IsIt: clubs). Play: player to dealer's left leads; must follow suit when possible; trick won by highest card of led suit or highest trump. Trick winner leads next.",
    Player: "After the deal, bidding starts with the player to dealer's left. Each player may bid once (or pass). Bids in ascending order: Question, IsIt, Kicker, Having the Ladies, Solo, IsIt Solo, 6 Trick Solo, Bronco, Bull Solo, Solo 2. Highest bidder becomes declarer; in some bids the declarer calls an ace (not in hand) and its holder is partner. Trump is determined by the bid (e.g. Solo: declarer chooses; IsIt: clubs). Play: player to dealer's left leads; must follow suit when possible; trick won by highest card of led suit or highest trump. Trick winner leads next.",
    objective: 'As declarer (alone or with a called partner), make your contract: win the agreed number of tricks (e.g. 5 for Question/IsIt/Ladies/Solo, 6 for 6 Trick Solo, 8 for Bull Solo or Solo 2). As defenders, set the declarer by preventing the contract.',
    gameplay: "After the deal, bidding starts with the player to dealer's left. Each player may bid once (or pass). Bids in ascending order: Question, IsIt, Kicker, Having the Ladies, Solo, IsIt Solo, 6 Trick Solo, Bronco, Bull Solo, Solo 2. Highest bidder becomes declarer; in some bids the declarer calls an ace (not in hand) and its holder is partner. Trump is determined by the bid (e.g. Solo: declarer chooses; IsIt: clubs). Play: player to dealer's left leads; must follow suit when possible; trick won by highest card of led suit or highest trump. Trick winner leads next.",
    keyRules: [
      'Top three trumps are fixed: Queen of Clubs (highest), 7 of trump (second), Queen of Spades (third).',
      'Must follow suit when possible.',
      'Bidder or partners must make the contracted number of tricks to score; otherwise defenders score.',
      'In Kicker and Bronco the declarer must take zero tricks.',
    ],
    bonusRuleGuids: [],
    useTrump: true,
