      equipment: 'Standard playing cards; optionally chips or money for scoring.',
      dealing: "Deal 8 cards each (4 players). A 3-2-3 or similar pattern; dealing starts to dealer's left. Dealer must verify each player has 8 cards before turning cards or a misdeal may be called. Deal rotates left after each hand.",
    },
    turnFlow: "After the deal, bidding starts with the player to dealer's left. Each player may bid once (or pass). Bids in ascending order: Question, IsIt, Kicker, Having the Ladies, Solo, IsIt Solo, 6 Trick Solo, Bronco, Bull Solo, Solo 2. Highest bidder becomes declarer; in some bids the declarer calls an ace (not in hand) and its holder is partner. Trump is determined by the bid (e.g. Solo: declarer chooses; IsIt: clubs). Play: player to dealer's left leads; must follow suit when possible; trick won by highest card of led suit or highest trump. Trick winner leads next.",
