    exampleHands: [
      'Setup example: 8 card(s) per player.',
      'Rule example: As declarer (alone or with a called partner), make your contract: win the agreed number of tricks (e.g. 5 for Question/IsIt/Ladies/Solo, 6 for 6 Trick Solo, 8 for Bull Solo or Solo 2). As defenders, set the declarer by preventing the contract.',
      "Turn-flow example: After the deal, bidding starts with the player to dealer's left. Each player may bid once (or pass). Bids in ascending order: Question, IsIt, Kicker, Having the Ladies, Solo, IsIt Solo, 6 Trick Solo, Bronco, Bull Solo, Solo 2. Highest bidder becomes declarer; in some bids the declarer calls an ace (not in hand) and its holder is partner. Trump is determined by the bid (e.g. Solo: declarer chooses; IsIt: clubs). Play: player to dealer's left leads; must follow suit when possible; trick won by highest card of led suit or highest trump. Trick winner leads next.",
      'Scoring example: Score by bid value (e.g. Nickel Solo: bid value times 5 cents per opponent). Declarer pays each opponent if set; opponents pay declarer if contract is made. Mackers and First/Last add bonuses. Declarer (and partner if applicable) must win the contracted number of tricks (e.g. 5 for Question/IsIt/Solo, 6 for 6 Trick Solo, 8 for Bull Solo). If successful, declarer scores; otherwise defenders score..',
